 Non-goals\nDeciding where assurance and history-author-acknowledge land is the delivery task filed beside this issue; deciding init/config/schema/profile stays pm-npr3."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:sdk","cli","contracts","gate","governance","grammar"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-09-12T19:57:52.201Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-12T19:57:52.201Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":180},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"verifyPmCliGrammar or the command-grammar gate reports a terminal_consolidation_owner finding when a consolidation row's owner is closed, canceled or missing and the command is not carried by the alias relocation table, with a negative-control fixture; config, profile, schema and init rows name pm-npr3; assurance and history-author-acknowledge rows name the open delivery task filed beside this issue; the contracts fixture is regenerated; The gate's negative control proves a stale-owner row fails upward in CI"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-n7rr"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Every consolidation row names an open owner or is reclassified; the grammar verification reports a finding when a consolidation owner is terminal or unknown."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"assurance, config, profile, schema name closed pm-6apl; history-author-acknowledge names closed pm-tqel; init names the epic instead of pm-npr3; no check reads owner status."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadat